# playpick cell: mode=daily boss=host (coverage label only -- daily.boss is
# not a real playpick axis, the actual daily is whatever the date computes)
# spec=druid:feral style=dodge view=1280x800 save=fresh.
#
# Probed first (2026-09-29-4-probe.play): today's actual daily is The Skyward
# Deck, 25-player heroic, HASTENED -- the same instance four 2026-09-28
# sessions already fought (good x2, mash, wander), all melee/caster styles
# that press a rotation. No session has run `dodge` against this fight, and
# no daily session has ever picked a druid (checked sessions.jsonl: every
# prior daily spec was warrior, paladin, priest, shaman, hunter or warlock).
# dodge presses nothing and steers only away from telegraphs, so this tests
# whether hypothesis 1 ("doing nothing wins") still holds on the roster's
# single largest played/idle gap (docs/upkeep.md: played 76% / idle 6%,
# +70) and on a fight with a fixed-schedule enrage rather than a boss-health
# gate -- the 2026-09-27 dodge-vs-Three-Crowns pull found the opposite shape
# there (dodge got furthest of any style, then died anyway to an enrage with
# no damage dealer). Class grid tile confirmed via probe screenshot:
# class:10 reads "Druid Feral" at both 390-wide (3-column) and 1280-wide
# (5-column) layouts, so the flat index is layout-independent.
open
tap daily
tap class:10
targets
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
bill

play dodge 90
state
shot mid1
